<title>SOUTH KOREA: Trading still halted in Dongshin.</title>
<headline>Trading still halted in Dongshin.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading remained halted in South Korea's Dongshin Construction Co Ltd on Monday after the company announced it had defaulted on payments of debt worth 17.8 billion won.</p>
<p>On Saturday the stock exchange froze trading in the construction company, citing rumours of a debt default.</p>
<p>Dongshin issued a statement saying it had missed payments on corporate bonds worth 10.3 billion won and promissary notes of 7.5 billion won.</p>
<p>The company had applied for court receivership on Friday, the statement said.</p>
</text>
